  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improving the Evidence Base on Intentions, Awareness and Decision-Making on Irregular Migration in Lebanon</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Lebanon&#x2019;s severe economic deterioration has triggered unprecedented levels of poverty, prompting rising despair and frustration across all population groups. Economic difficulties are rendering living conditions in Lebanon untenable and compelling an increasing number to seek routes out of Lebanon in search of better lives. The situation in Lebanon, in addition to the limited regular migration pathways mean Lebanon is seeing a sharp rise in irregular migration to Europe. This research project seeks to improve knowledge and understanding of irregular migration intentions, awareness around regular migration pathways, and decision-making factors in the Lebanese context. Two reports are being developed. Both the inception report and the final report will act as an anchor for IOM to engage partners, reflect on programming and research approach, and adapt response methods to the growing trend of irregular migration in Lebanon.</narrative>
  </description>
